ia/denmark">Denmark</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalmar-union">Kalmar Union</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1536</span><span class="rf-text">Christian III introduces the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Lutheran Reformation</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1658</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-roskilde">Treaty of Roskilde</a> cedes <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scania">Scania</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/halland">Halland</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/blekinge">Blekinge</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1814</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-kiel">Treaty of Kiel</a> transfers <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1849</span><span class="rf-text">The Constitution of 5 June ends absolute monarchy</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1864</span><span class="rf-text">Defeat in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-schleswig-war">Second Schleswig War</a> costs <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schleswig">Schleswig</a> and Holstein</span></li></ol>
